WHAT THIS PROVES AND WHAT IT DOES NOT: check.py rejects a plural selector that
is not a category of the locale, and a plural without `other`
(scripts/i18n/check.py:_check_plural_categories). It does NOT require the locale's
full category set — an es plural missing `many` passes it — and it never looks at
what a branch RENDERS. Section A of the probe therefore adds full one/many/other
coverage and per-branch argument parity, which the validator cannot see.

